    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0354" n="328" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v10/pg328"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Truman
                    Library, Truman papers, PSF–Subject
                    file</note>
                <head>No. 147<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by J. S. Earman, Executive Assistant to the Director
                        of Central Intelligence, to Rear Admiral R. L.
                            Dennison, Naval Aide to the President</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-01-18">18 January 1952</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Director of Central Intelligence asks that the attached memorandum be shown
                    to the President.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d147-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. S.
                                Earman</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d147-a1.xml" xpointer="d147-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d147-f1" n="1" xml:id="d147-f1-content">
                <p>The following handwritten notation appears on the source text: “I do not think
                    that we should make this advance now. H[arry] S.
                        T[ruman]”. The following typed notation also appears on the
                    source text: “1–25–52—President said he talked to the Secy. of State—no letter
                    necessary. Rose A. C[onway].” For the Department of State
                    instructions to Tehran conveying the President’s wishes, see <ref target="#d152"
                        >Document 152</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
